## New ideas added

- **IPL Team Owner: Where Does the Money Actually Come From?** — Hook: 'IPL team kharidne ke ₹1,000+ crore lagte hain. Owner ko wapas kaise milta hai?' Payoff: follow ₹100 of IPL revenue and show the central-pool share, how little comes from tickets, and where it goes (player purse, ops). Then show the real payoff, which is brand value. _(pattern: Follow one rupee through a dream-to-own business, and reveal that the obvious income source (tickets) is the smallest slice.; evidence: )_
- **₹500 Ki Beer Pub Mein: Bar Owner Ko Kitna Bachta Hai?** — Hook: 'Wine shop pe beer ₹180, pub mein ₹500. Fark kiske paas jaata hai?' Payoff: break the ₹500 into the liquor cost, licence and excise burden, rent and staff, leaving the owner's margin. Show why pubs are packed on weekends and still struggle. _(pattern: Price-gap reveal: the same product at two prices, then show who gets the difference.; evidence: )_
- **Airport Pe ₹250 Ki Chai: Dukaan Wale Ko Kitna Bachta Hai?** — Hook: 'Airport pe chai ₹250 kyun? Dukaan wala loot raha hai?' Payoff: the outlet gives a big share of every sale to the airport operator and still has to staff it 24x7. Show how much of the ₹250 is left. The twist is that the outlet owner is not the villain. _(pattern: 'Why is this so expensive?' myth-bust, where the obvious villain turns out to be squeezed too.; evidence: )_
- **₹1,200/Hour JCB Rent: Machine Kitne Ghante Chalke Paisa Wapas Deti Hai?** — Hook: 'Ek JCB ₹30 lakh ki. Roz kitne ghante chalni chahiye ki EMI nikle?' Payoff: a break-even hours-per-month calculation, then what happens when she idles for 2 monsoon months. Show who actually profits: the owner with 3+ machines and steady contractor tie-ups. _(pattern: Break-even counter: 'how many X before you make ₹1 of profit' applied to a heavy asset.; evidence: )_
- **₹1 Lakh Coaching Fee: Institute Owner Ke Paas Kitna Bachta Hai?** — Hook: 'Ek batch mein 100 bachche, ₹1 lakh fee. ₹1 crore aaya. Owner ke haath mein kitna?' Payoff: line up the costs (star faculty cut, rent, ads, staff) and show the margin. Then show why the real money is in the top-rank marketing machine and not in teaching. _(pattern: Per-customer revenue to take-home, applied to a business with a huge emotional pull (parents' money, kids' futures).; evidence: )_
- **₹500 Ki Cab Ride: Driver, Fleet Owner Aur App Ko Kitna Milta Hai?** — Hook: 'Aapne ₹500 ka cab liya. Driver ke haath mein kitna aaya?' Payoff: split one ₹500 ride across the app, the owner's EMI and the driver's fuel, with the driver's real hourly earning at the end. Compare driver-owner vs fleet-owner economics. _(pattern: Split-the-ticket: one transaction we all make, shown as slices that go to different people.; evidence: )_
